  "id": "COMPOUND:28122 - PROTEIN:1026",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that [(Z)-(3-hydroxy-4-methoxyphenyl)methylideneamino]thiourea acts as a target for multiple potassium channel subfamily members, which in turn target Cyclin-dependent kinase inhibitor 1. This relationship is supported by the presence of a common intermediate, [(1S,2S,4R,7E,10R,11R)-4,8-dimethyl-12-methylidene-13-oxo-3,14-dioxatricyclo[9.3.0.02,4]tetradec-7-en-10-yl] acetate, which is a known target of several compounds, including the thiourea derivative. The shared mechanism of targeting potassium channels and their downstream effect on cyclin-dependent kinase inhibitors implies a potential pathway where the thiourea compound may modulate cellular processes through potassium channel activity, ultimately influencing the activity of cyclin-dependent kinase inhibitors. The evidence is consistent across multiple paths, highlighting a possible role in the regulation of cell cycle progression through the interaction with these inhibitors.",
